@misc{xue2026from, title = {From Correctness to Consistency: Redefining Reliability for the Agentware Era}, author = {Qin, Xue and Gruppi, Maurício}, year = {2026}, eprint = {2611.27829}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, url = {https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.27829} }
We introduce Differential Logic Analysis (DLA), a framework that utilizes Logical Inference to detect internal contradictions across parallel and sequential development workflows. Preliminary simulations demonstrate that DLA successfully intercepts logic drift, such as contradictions and unspecified assumptions, and offers a new perspective on reliability assessment in the AI-assistant development era.
